From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:46:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 208/208] avcodec: add V4L2 Request API MPEG-4 Part 2, H.263
 and Sorenson Spark hwaccels

Add hwaccels for the proposed V4L2 stateless MPEG-4 Part 2, H.263 and
Sorenson Spark decoder API: the MG4S, S263 and SPKS pixel formats with
the MPEG4_VOL, MPEG4_VOP, MPEG4_QUANTISATION, MPEG4_QUIRKS and
H263_PICTURE controls, and the optional MPEG4_SLICE_PARAMS and
H263_SLICE_PARAMS arrays for drivers which cannot parse video packet,
GOB or slice headers (HWACCEL_CAP_RESYNC_SLICES). A private copy of the
uAPI is used until it is in the kernel headers.

The output buffer gets the VOP or picture from its start code, without
the VOL, GOV or user data which may precede it, and only that VOP of a
packed DivX frame.

The encoder bugs detected by ff_mpeg4_workaround_bugs() which matter to
the reconstruction of the stream are passed as quirks; when the driver
cannot reproduce one of them, or the stream uses tools outside of the
Simple and Advanced Simple profiles, init() fails and the decoder falls
back to software. The H263_PICTURE control of the first picture is set
in init(), so that the driver can refuse the H.263 modes it lacks
before decoding starts.

Tested with the Cedrus driver on Allwinner H616.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
